WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.067 --> 00:00:10.614
Hi there!

2
00:00:10.615 --> 00:00:13.066
Hi there!

3
00:00:13.066 --> 00:00:15.942
Who are you?

4
00:00:15.942 --> 00:00:18.891
I'm a moose.

5
00:00:18.891 --> 00:00:24.269
Moose are the biggest kind of deer.

6
00:00:24.269 --> 00:00:26.485
Where do you live?

7
00:00:26.485 --> 00:00:30.491
Moose live in cold parts of the world.

8
00:00:30.491 --> 00:00:33.428
We like forests.

9
00:00:33.428 --> 00:00:39.080
We stay near lakes, ponds, or streams.

10
00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:41.347
Can you swim?

11
00:00:41.347 --> 00:00:45.425
Yes, we're great swimmers.

12
00:00:45.425 --> 00:00:50.213
We can also run fast.

13
00:00:50.213 --> 00:00:52.880
It's cold here!

14
00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:56.477
Moose love the cold.

15
00:00:56.477 --> 00:01:00.012
Our fur keeps us warm.

16
00:01:00.013 --> 00:01:05.400
Our hooves help us walk in snow.

17
00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:08.346
What do you eat?

18
00:01:08.347 --> 00:01:11.179
Moose don't eat meat.

19
00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:17.043
We eat twigs, bark, leaves, and pinecones.

20
00:01:17.043 --> 00:01:21.815
We also eat plants that grow in water.

21
00:01:21.816 --> 00:01:25.234
You have big antlers!

22
00:01:25.234 --> 00:01:28.930
My antlers fall off each year.

23
00:01:28.930 --> 00:01:32.968
Then they grow back—even bigger.

24
00:01:32.968 --> 00:01:38.124
We use antlers to find mates and fight.

25
00:01:38.124 --> 00:01:40.566
Who do you fight?

26
00:01:40.566 --> 00:01:43.660
Male moose fight each other.

27
00:01:43.660 --> 00:01:47.610
We also fight enemies.

28
00:01:47.610 --> 00:01:55.179
Bears, wolves, and cougars hunt us.

29
00:01:55.179 --> 00:01:58.163
I'm going for a swim now.

30
00:01:58.163 --> 00:02:01.775
I'll see you later.

31
00:02:01.776 --> 00:02:07.940
Good-bye, Moose!
